From 92e9ff987d19fc2259552312faad3ecf2b1537a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Roscoe <bryanroscoe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:25:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/30] Costs: tap a source before sacrificing it to its own
 activation

Hashep Oasis: "{1}{G}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice a Desert: Target creature gets
+3/+3 until end of turn. Activate only as a sorcery." The Oasis is itself
a Desert, and the ruling allows sacrificing it to its own ability.

CR 601.2h + CR 602.2b: the costs of an activated ability may be paid in
any order. phase offered the Oasis as the Desert, sacrificed it, and then
refused the activation because the {T} source had left the battlefield
(costs.rs, "source is not on the battlefield"). When the selected
permanent is the ability's own source and the remaining cost taps it,
handle_sacrifice_for_cost now taps it first, through the single tap
authority, and removes the {T} leg from the residual.

Test: tests/integration/hashep_oasis_sacrifices_itself.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
